    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Well, I believe the dream is still alive. We got past the six to four super ranks, a year later, the passage of the voting ranks, a six to five. And we made so much progress. We come such a distance. And when I hear people saying nothing has changed, I feel like saying comment and walk in my shoes. I grew up in rural Alabama, tennis school in Tennessee, lived in Georgia the past 51 years. And when I was growing up, I saw those signs that said white men, colored men, white women, colored women, white weighting, colored weighting. Those signs are gone and they will not return. The only places our children and their children will see those signs today will be in a book, in a museum, on a video.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
