    "turn_text": "It is not so much a burden, but I feel like I have an obligation, a mission to do what I can, to continue to tell the story, and to be a witness, just to be a witness. A set of people, this is what happened, this is how it happened, and we made progress, but we're not quite there yet. We have to continue to work to lay down the burden of race and create what Dr. King called the beloved community, for we respect the dignity and the worth of every human being. And it doesn't matter whether we are black or white, Latino, Asian, America, a Native American. We are one people. We are one family. We are one house. We all live in the American house or the world house.",
