  {
    "episode_id": 86732,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 57,
    "turn_text": "Or if the Civil Rights Bill or the Voting Rights Act was before the Congress today, I think it would be almost impossible to get it passed. In the Congress, like in the great part of America, I think we need to, again, teach people the way of peace, the way of law, the way of nonviolence. Is it possible for us to come together again and look out for all of our citizens? Is it possible for us to have companies that immigration reform and not leave millions and millions of human beings living in fear?",
