  {
    "episode_id": 86732,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 76,
    "turn_text": "It freed me. It liberated me. It made me a better human being. You have to be prepared to stand up for what you believe in. to speak up, speak out, and be prepared to give it your all. But we've been on a freedom ride. We've prepared to die. Not just to give a little blood, but prepare to die, to desegregate public transportation in the American South. Some people said that we should cool off, that we should end the freedom ride, but we couldn't. You have to go on and see what the end is going to be. You have to be hopeful and optimistic that all is going to work out. That's what I believe then. That's what I believe now.",
