  {
    "episode_id": 86732,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 79,
    "turn_text": "You've been listening to Representative John Lewis, one of our country's most important civil rights leaders. Welcome to this dialogue extra on Marcia Franklin. In 2014, I talk with Representative John Lewis of Georgia at the Sun Valley Writers Conference. The last of the so-called big six leaders of the civil rights movement, Lewis had embarked on a new adventure. The writing of a trilogy of comic books about his life called March. The first book in the series had hit number one on the New York Times bestsellers list. Now the person with the idea for the series was Andrew Iden, a young staffer for Lewis and a comic book fan. I found his own story compelling, so we sat down for this interview. So tell me how this idea came to you for this comic book with the Congressman.",
