  {
    "episode_id": 86732,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 80,
    "turn_text": "I was serving as his press secretary on his 2008 reelection campaign. And one of the things when you work with him is you see him tell these stories to young people, and you see the way they react. And the way it inspires them, it pushes them to do new things and to look at things in a different way. And so it was coming down to the end of the campaign. And I'm a pretty big comic book fan. And people were talking about what they were going to do after the campaign was over. And they said the usual things. I'm going to go to the beach. I'm going to go see my parents. And I said, I'm going to go to a comic book convention. And Congressman said, you know, There was a comic book during the movement. It was incredibly influential. It was called Martin Luther King in the Montgomery story.",
