    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 85,
    "turn_text": "You see those two pieces and it's almost right there. Congressman Lewis was a part of so many pivotal moments of direct action during the civil rights movement. Stories that are often forgotten today. And when they were told, people look at their history in a whole new way. And so I just started asking. I was 24 years old. I didn't know any better. And I said, Congressman, why don't you write a comic book? And finally he said, I will, but only if you write it with me.",
