  {
    "episode_id": 86732,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 97,
    "turn_text": "Well, I grew up in Atlanta, like I said, and Congressman was my Congressman. And I had gone to work in Connecticut. I had graduated from college up there and had been in politics. But as a young person, my father left when I was about three. And so I was raised by a single mother. And at the same time after he left, when I started getting into comics, you're searching for role models, you're searching for heroes, you're searching for people who are interested in right injustice. And that's how I fell in love with comics. And so when I went to school in Connecticut, I started working in politics. I was the floor assistant lieutenant governor there at the state senate and then went on to work for another member. And I started in the congressman's office answering mail. And sort of worked my way up from there.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
