    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 103,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. People don't know this truth today in many cases. My generation doesn't know the truth of the brutality of the disrespect that was so often accepted as universal behavior in many places. And so when it came time to make those decisions, the answer was always very simple. It was tell it like it was. Make it plain. Show them what this life was so that they can understand where we came from, so that these young people, these readers, people who are not so young, who maybe have forgotten this period of time, can come to understand and remember the challenges, the disrespect, the brutality, the suffering, and all that was given to right those wrongs.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
