  {
    "episode_id": 86732,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 105,
    "turn_text": "You know, I think it's not just my generation, but certainly my generation have grown up with social media. I think we've become somewhat complacent. We're satisfied to click like and we're satisfied to retweet and consider that our full measure of devotion that we can offer. When, in fact, we need to be using these tools to organize, to put our bodies on the line, to once again show our commitment to what we believe in, not simply by taking a indirect action, but by taking direct action. And then, you know, hopefully These graphic novels will stand beyond simply my generation, but will extend to subsequent generations who will continue to learn these lessons and continue to understand nonviolence as vital and important tool and hopefully as a way of living their life. Because if they do, then this world is going to be a more peaceful and just place to live in.",
