    "turn_text": "nerd, as some people say. And so I wrote my grad school thesis about that comic book. And it was one of the first definitive histories written. My thesis advisor at Georgetown certainly gave me an odd look when I first suggested writing it on the comic book. But after a while after I explained it, she thought it was absolutely vital that I continue this research. And so that thesis then ended up becoming an article that we published in a newspaper in Atlanta when we first released March, and it showed people that this had been done before. And then everybody started asking, Colbert had it on the big screen when the congressman went on, and to bring it back into print then seemed like the inevitable next step. And I think it serves as a very important stepping stone into this history. In a sense, that's the first chapter, and March is the next chapter.",
