    "turn_text": "No, the hardest part is actually figuring out who drew it. Nobody knows who the artist is. We figured out who the writer was. It was a collaboration by Benton Resnick and Alfred Hasseler. But the Fellowship of Reconciliation, the organization that originally published it, was more than happy to bring back a new printing and to work with us to get it out there, put it on Amazon, put it in comic book stores. I think we see comic stores around nowadays and you've got Spider-Man and Batman and then now Dr. King and John Lewis. And that's a huge shift. This was be considered 10 years ago, public information comics, and now they're considered cutting edge.",
