    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 121,
    "turn_text": "It was apparently somewhat over 100 people camped out to see the panel, which I'd been going to comics as a fan. So this was my first time ever going to a comic convention as a creator. And I just never forget seeing that line of people just waiting and then cheering when we got there. And it was unreal. I finally got to make my comic book jokes to people and they laughed. And then, you know, the most meaningful moment was when the teachers got up and they started asking questions and they never got to their question because they were crying saying to the congressman and to us that this is something they needed. They needed it so badly so that they had the tools in their classroom to show the next generation what they needed, the shoes that they were walking in and what they needed to do.",
