  },
  {
    "episode_id": 86732,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 134,
    "turn_text": "Absolutely. I mean, I think we're ripe. People are frustrated. People want to do something and they want to know how it was done before. And so I think that partially drove the interest. I think there's also a lesson in this about sticking to your guns and doing what you believed in. If folks are laughing at you, it probably means you're doing something right. the courage to see outside of the box as Congressman Lewis has his whole life and to embrace new ideas, sometimes to embrace reinvented ideas that perhaps have been done before, but to follow your dreams. I mean, when we started this, I had no idea. It was just an idea. We worked on it for five years before it was released. And then I'll never forget when we found out it was going to be number one that Congressman and I hugged and we both cried a little bit. It was just one of those moments in your life. You only hope that you get to live. And I'll always treasure that time.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_00",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
