    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/6/86732.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 139,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and they're very active still. I think it's one of those organizations that people think of in the previous context, but Kristen Stone King was one of the folks who helped organize the UC Davis protests. She's the new executive director. I remember that was where they were maced so savagely. And now you've got them reengaging on a national level. And, you know, they sort of joked that this was the biggest fundraiser they'd had since we released this comic book. But that's because nobody's investing in peace activities. And hopefully, this changes that conversation and shows people that those activities pay dividends. And sometimes those dividends are 50 years later. You just don't know where they'll show up.",
